Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Fast Gates on a Transmon", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A transmon is a superconducting circuit that behaves as a weakly anharmonic \
oscillator. A qubit is stored in its two lowest levels, and a microwave pulse \
at the qubit frequency rotates it between them. The anharmonicity is small, a \
few hundred megahertz against a qubit frequency of several gigahertz, so the \
transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],
 " lies close to the qubit transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 ". A short pulse has a broad spectrum and drives both transitions, carrying \
population out of the qubit. It must also be strong to complete the rotation \
in time. A strong drive couples ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 " and pushes the energy of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],
 ", which moves the qubit transition away from the drive frequency, so the \
rotation misses its target unless the pulse's amplitude and frequency are \
calibrated. A long pulse avoids both problems but is exposed for longer to \
energy decay and dephasing."
}], "Text",
 CellID->329621944,ExpressionUUID->"56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The gate studied here flips the qubit, taking ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],
 ". It rotates the qubit by an angle \[Pi], so it is called a \[Pi] pulse. \
The population a pulse carries out of the qubit, mostly into ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 ", is called leakage. A correction known as DRAG (derivative removal by \
adiabatic gate) reduces it by adding a second drive to the pulse."
}], "Text",
 CellID->515379898,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For a given pulse shape, how long the best \[Pi] pulse is, and how much \
DRAG shortens it, has no exact closed-form answer. Both follow from the Schr\
\[ODoubleDot]dinger and Lindblad equations solved with the levels the qubit \
leaks into kept explicitly, and with the amplitude, frequency and DRAG \
coefficient of the pulse calibrated together with its length. For an \
anharmonicity of \[Minus]200 MHz and coherence times ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "1"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["T", "TI"], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " of 100 \[Mu]s, DRAG lets the pulse shrink until energy decay and dephasing \
alone set its error. Without DRAG the pulse must stay long enough for leakage \
to die out, and its best error is larger."
}], "Text",
 CellID->604760901,ExpressionUUID->"6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],

Cell["The Driven Transmon", "Section",
 CellID->1476799103,ExpressionUUID->"569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],

Cell["\<\
The transmon is well approximated by an anharmonic oscillator. It is driven \
by a microwave pulse near its qubit frequency, with a DRAG correction added \
to the pulse:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->448336599,ExpressionUUID->"15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["lab",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", "[", 
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "-", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
      OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "."], 
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], "]", "(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->970785311,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first two terms describe the transmon, and the last term is the drive. \
Here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["b", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],
 " lowers the number of excitations by one, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["q", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " is the qubit frequency and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 " is the anharmonicity. For a transmon ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],
 " is negative: the transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " lies ",
 Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
    {
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}
   },
   GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],
 " below the qubit transition."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1377816002,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive oscillates at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]], "-", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],
 ", detuned from the qubit by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],
 ", and its envelope ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " sets its strength. The detuning lets the drive follow the qubit \
transition. The second term in the bracket is the DRAG correction. It \
oscillates as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["sin",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 " instead of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["cos",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],
 ", and its strength follows the slope of the envelope, scaled by the DRAG \
coefficient ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],
 ". Dividing the slope by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],
 " gives it the units of ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[CapitalOmega]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],
 ", so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],
 " is a pure number. For a weak drive and no detuning, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],
 " removes the component of the drive at the leakage frequency. At ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 " the correction is off and the pulse is a plain microwave drive. The \
amplitude of the envelope, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],
 " are the three controls of the pulse."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1439899046,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive is simplest to describe in a frame rotating with it, which \
subtracts ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " for every excitation. In the rotating frame, some drive terms vary only \
with the pulse envelope. Others oscillate at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 ", much faster than the envelope and populations change. These fast terms \
largely average out when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "\[LessLess]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 "; dropping them is the rotating-wave approximation. What remains is the \
Hamiltonian used throughout:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1641200340,ExpressionUUID->"034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   FractionBox[
    StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"], "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "(", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"]}], ")", "-", 
   FractionBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     OverscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "."], 
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"2", 
     StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], "(", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
    StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], ")"}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1424533854,ExpressionUUID->"52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In this frame the first two terms set the energies of the levels, and the \
last two couple neighboring levels. To write these terms as matrices, the \
oscillator is truncated to its five lowest levels, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"0"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"4"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", which hold the qubit and the levels it leaks into; the last section \
checks how many levels are needed."
}], "Text",
 CellID->535457321,ExpressionUUID->"2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],

Cell["Define the lowering operator of a five-level oscillator:", "Text",
 CellID->141959522,ExpressionUUID->"6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"b", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"AnnihilationOperator", "[", "5", "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->299517738,ExpressionUUID->"608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The drive couples neighboring levels with strengths 1, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox["2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SqrtBox["3"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],
 " and 2, so it drives the transition from ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"1"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 " to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"2"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],
 " more strongly than the qubit transition:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2142391071,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"MatrixForm", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"b", " ", "+", " ", 
     RowBox[{"b", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}], "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"",
    "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->1002769646,ExpressionUUID->"2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The envelope is a raised cosine of length ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],
 " and amplitude ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],
 ". It and its slope vanish at both ends, so the DRAG term also starts and \
ends at zero, and at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "=", "1"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " its area is ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->436346740,ExpressionUUID->"14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"envelope", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"A", " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "\[Tau]"}], ")"}], " ", 
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", 
      RowBox[{"2", " ", "Pi", " ", 
       RowBox[{"t", "/", "\[Tau]"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->2122865143,ExpressionUUID->"5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Write ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 " for any lowering operator ",
 Cell[BoxData["c"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 ", so that the number of kept levels can be changed later:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1735808809,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"hamiltonian", "[", "c_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", " ", "@", " ", "c"}]}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Delta]", " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "@", " ", "c"}], 
      ")"}]}], " ", "+", "\n", "   ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"envelope", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"c", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"D", "[", 
         RowBox[{"envelope", ",", " ", "t"}], "]"}], "/", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Alpha]"}], ")"}]}]}], ")"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"I", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"c", "[", "\"\<Dagger\>\"", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "c"}], 
        ")"}]}], ")"}]}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->753514147,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Make ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["H", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " for five levels one operator. Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Parameters\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],
 " list fixes the order in which numbers are supplied: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Alpha]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Tau]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1164297175,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"model", " ", "=", " ", 
